Z||000000||grinthock||07-28-2001||08:03 AM||||I know this has been brought up before but the questions are not really answered.....<P>1)  I understand that chips in a Fiero do almost nothing because our STOCK ECM is the "best" and is already setup perfect, or this is what they say<P>2)  I have some mods, intake, cam, ported exhaust.<P>3)  Would a performance chip do ANYTHING?  Honestly does anyone have one and notice a difference??<P>Thanks guys||||reg||1
Z||000001||Shaun41178||07-28-2001||11:39 AM||||a chip made for a stock v6 won't do anything.  with the mods you have you will need to get a custom tuned prom for your car to get the best improvement.  Don't waste your money on those hypertech crap things.  Waste of money.  maybe 1-2 hp increase peak and that is way in the top end and you need to run premium fuel.  hehe no thanks.<P>What you will need to do is hit a dyno and have someone there with the equipment to burn new chips and change parameters to find the best combo.  This of course takes quite a bit of dyno time and yes that is expensive.<P>I say forget the chip idea.  If you don't have a pulley then get one of those and then a ported TB and intake manifold, and a good cat-back or something.  around 2.5 inches or so.  Pulley itself will add more then a chip will.  ported TB will add about 4 hp and around 3 torque.  gasket match the upper plenum to the TB and you will get about a 7 hp increase over stock and around 5-7 torque.<P><P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dave Gunsul||07-29-2001||03:04 AM||||A custom chip is the best route to take.<BR>A custom chip is taylor made for your car and it's mods but they are very expensive.<BR>Superchips makes custom chips for any car.<P>I must say again though,even though a lot of people get mad because one worked for me, that my ADS chip did in fact make a difference in my car. No I don't have a dyno,<BR>or any real proof, but I know my car and it is faster with the chip than without it.<P>&lt;now sitting in a tub full of icewater awaiting the flames&gt;  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
